    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nVelocity drops from u to u/2 in s\u2081 = 3 cm. Total stopping distance s_total = u\u00b2 / (2a). For first 3 cm: (u/2)\u00b2 = u\u00b2 - 2a(3) => u\u00b2/4 = u\u00b2 - 6a => 6a = 3u\u00b2/4 => 2a = u\u00b2/4. s_total = u\u00b2 / (2a) = u\u00b2 / (u\u00b2/4) = 4 cm. Additional distance = 4 - 3 = 1 cm.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nu\u2081 = u, v\u2081 = u/2, s\u2081 = 3 cm.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nv\u00b2 = u\u00b2 - 2as => s_total = 4/3 s\u2081 = 4 cm; \u0394s = 4 - 3 = 1 cm\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. In the first 3 cm: v\u2081\u00b2 = u\u00b2 - 2 a s\u2081 => (u/2)\u00b2 = u\u00b2 - 2a(3).\n2. u\u00b2 / 4 = u\u00b2 - 6a => 6a = 3u\u00b2 / 4 => 2a = u\u00b2 / 4.\n3. Total penetration to complete stop (v = 0):\n   0 = u\u00b2 - 2 a s_total => s_total = u\u00b2 / (2a) = u\u00b2 / (u\u00b2 / 4) = 4 cm.\n4. Additional distance penetrated = s_total - s\u2081 = 4 cm - 3 cm = 1 cm.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 1 cm\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nClassic NEET bullet problem: Halving velocity uses up 75% of kinetic energy, so only 25% of penetration remains: 3 cm covers 75%, so 1 cm covers the remaining 25%!",
