    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nAt t = 8 s, the ball inherits horizontal speed v_x = at = 5 \u00d7 8 = 40 m/s. Once released, v_x remains 40 m/s. In \u0394t = 1 s, vertical velocity becomes v_y = g \u0394t = 10 \u00d7 1 = 10 m/s. Net velocity v = \u221a(v_x\u00b2 + v_y\u00b2) = \u221a(40\u00b2 + 10\u00b2) = \u221a1700 \u2248 41.23 m/s.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nCar: u = 0, a = 5 m/s\u00b2, t = 8 s. Ball dropped at t = 8 s, observed at t = 9 s. g = 10 m/s\u00b2.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nv_x = a t; v_y = g \u0394t; v = \u221a(v_x\u00b2 + v_y\u00b2)\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Horizontal velocity acquired by car (and inherited by ball) at t = 8 s:\n   v_x = 0 + a t = 5 \u00d7 8 = 40 m/s.\n2. Since gravity acts purely vertically, the horizontal velocity remains constant: v_x = 40 m/s.\n3. At t = 9 s, time elapsed since release is \u0394t = 9 s - 8 s = 1 s.\n4. Downward vertical velocity gained under gravity: v_y = g \u0394t = 10 \u00d7 1 = 10 m/s.\n5. Magnitude of resultant velocity: v = \u221a(v_x\u00b2 + v_y\u00b2) = \u221a(40\u00b2 + 10\u00b2) = \u221a(1600 + 100) = \u221a1700 \u2248 41.23 m/s.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption B: 41.2 m/s\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nNEET UG 2022 Official Paper Question! Don't forget that the dropped ball retains the horizontal speed of the vehicle!",
