    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nFor equal time intervals, average speed is the arithmetic mean: v_avg = (v\u2081 + v\u2082) / 2 = (40 + 60) / 2 = 50 m/s.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nEqual times: t\u2081 = t\u2082 = T/2, v\u2081 = 40 m/s, v\u2082 = 60 m/s.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nv_avg = (v\u2081 + v\u2082) / 2\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Total distance = s\u2081 + s\u2082 = v\u2081(T/2) + v\u2082(T/2) = (v\u2081 + v\u2082) T / 2.\n2. Average speed = Total Distance / Total Time = [(v\u2081 + v\u2082) T / 2] / T = (v\u2081 + v\u2082) / 2.\n3. v_avg = (40 + 60) / 2 = 50 m/s.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 50 m/s\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nEqual time intervals => Arithmetic Mean! Equal distance intervals => Harmonic Mean!",
