    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nv-t graph is a trapezoid: lower base b\u2081 = t + 2t + t = 4t. Upper base b\u2082 = 2t. Area = 1/2 (4t + 2t) v_max = 3t v_max. Average velocity = Area / Total Time = 3t v_max / 4t = 3/4 v_max.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nTimes: acceleration = t, constant velocity = 2t, deceleration = t.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nv_avg = [(b\u2081 + b\u2082) / (2 b\u2081)] \u00d7 v_max\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Total time T = t + 2t + t = 4t.\n2. Duration of constant velocity = 2t.\n3. Total displacement (area of trapezoid):\n   s = (1/2) \u00d7 (4t + 2t) \u00d7 v_max = (1/2) \u00d7 6t \u00d7 v_max = 3t v_max.\n4. Average velocity: v_avg = s / T = (3t v_max) / (4t) = (3/4) v_max.\n5. Ratio v_avg / v_max = 3 / 4.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 3 / 4\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nv_avg / v_max = (1 + t_const / T_total) / 2 = (1 + 2/4) / 2 = 1.5 / 2 = 3/4!",
