    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nWhen direction changes, total distance is the sum of magnitudes of displacements for each monotonic interval, whereas total displacement is simply x(t\u2082) - x(t\u2081).\n\n2. GIVEN:\nPosition equation x(t) = 20 + 8t - 2t\u00b2, interval t = 0 to t = 4 s.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nd = |x(t_turn) - x(0)| + |x(4) - x(t_turn)|\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Velocity v(t) = dx/dt = 8 - 4t. Setting v = 0 gives t = 2 s (turnaround point in [0, 4]).\n2. Position at t = 0: x(0) = 20 m.\n3. Position at turnaround t = 2 s: x(2) = 20 + 8(2) - 2(4) = 28 m.\n4. Position at t = 4 s: x(4) = 20 + 8(4) - 2(16) = 20 m.\n5. Distance = |28 - 20| + |20 - 28| = 8 m + 8 m = 16 m.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption C: 16 m\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nDisplacement is x(4) - x(0) = 20 - 20 = 0 m, but total distance traveled is 16 m.",
