    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nFor uniformly accelerated motion where initial velocity and acceleration have opposite signs, the particle stops and turns back at t = u/|a|.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nu = +30 m/s, a = -6 m/s\u00b2, total time t = 7 s.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nTurnaround at t = u/|a| = 5 s. Distance = d\u2081 + d\u2082; Displacement s = ut + (1/2)at\u00b2.\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Turnaround time: v = u + at = 30 - 6t = 0 => t = 5 s.\n2. Distance in first 5 s (forward): d\u2081 = u\u00b2 / (2|a|) = 30\u00b2 / (2 \u00d7 6) = 75 m.\n3. Motion in next 2 s (backward from rest): d\u2082 = (1/2)|a|(\u0394t)\u00b2 = (1/2)(6)(2)\u00b2 = 12 m.\n4. Total distance in 7 s = 75 + 12 = 87 m.\n5. Displacement in 7 s: s = ut + (1/2)at\u00b2 = 30(7) - 3(49) = 210 - 147 = +63 m.\n6. Ratio = Distance / |Displacement| = 87 / 63 = 29 / 21.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption B: 29 : 21\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nAlways split the motion into two intervals: before turnaround and after turnaround.",
