    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nAverage speed = total distance / total time; Average velocity = net displacement / total time.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nLeg 1: +4 m/s, 6 s. Leg 2: -2 m/s, 4 s. Leg 3: +3 m/s, 2 s. Total time = 12 s.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nv_avg_speed = \u03a3 |v_i| t_i / T; v_avg_vel = \u03a3 v_i t_i / T\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Displacements: s\u2081 = (+4)(6) = +24 m; s\u2082 = (-2)(4) = -8 m; s\u2083 = (+3)(2) = +6 m.\n2. Net displacement = 24 - 8 + 6 = +22 m.\n3. Distances: d\u2081 = 24 m; d\u2082 = 8 m; d\u2083 = 6 m. Total distance = 24 + 8 + 6 = 38 m.\n4. Total time = 6 + 4 + 2 = 12 s.\n5. Average speed = 38 / 12 = 3.17 m/s.\n6. Average velocity = 22 / 12 = 1.83 m/s.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: Average speed = 3.17 m/s, Average velocity = 1.83 m/s\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nAverage speed is scalar (path length), average velocity is vector (displacement).",
