    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nTotal distance is \u222b |v(t)| dt. We split the integral at the zeros of velocity: t = 2 s and t = 4 s.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nv(t) = t\u00b2 - 6t + 8, zeros at t = 2 and t = 4, interval [0, 5] s.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nd = |\u222b\u2080\u00b2 v dt| + |\u222b\u2082\u2074 v dt| + |\u222b\u2084\u2075 v dt|\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Indefinite integral: x(t) = t\u00b3/3 - 3t\u00b2 + 8t.\n2. x(0) = 0.\n3. x(2) = 8/3 - 12 + 16 = 20/3 m => d\u2081 = 20/3 m.\n4. x(4) = 64/3 - 48 + 32 = 16/3 m => d\u2082 = |16/3 - 20/3| = 4/3 m.\n5. x(5) = 125/3 - 75 + 40 = 20/3 m => d\u2083 = |20/3 - 16/3| = 4/3 m.\n6. Total distance = 20/3 + 4/3 + 4/3 = 28/3 \u2248 9.33 m.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 9.33 m\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nAlways split integration of speed into separate intervals where velocity maintains a constant sign.",
