    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nDistance fallen from rest is proportional to $t^2$. In half the total time, the body falls one-fourth of the total height.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nTotal height H, total time T, time elapsed t = T / 2.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nh_fallen = (1/2)gt\u00b2; Height from ground = H - h_fallen\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Total height H = (1/2) g T\u00b2.\n2. Distance fallen in time t = T/2: h_fallen = (1/2) g (T/2)\u00b2 = (1/4) [(1/2) g T\u00b2] = H / 4.\n3. Height above the ground = H - h_fallen = H - H/4 = 3H / 4.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 3H / 4 above the ground\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nBe careful with wording: 'distance fallen' is $H/4$, but 'height above the ground' is $3H/4$!",
