    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nTotal time is the sum of time taken by the stone to fall ($t_1$) and time taken by sound to travel up ($t_2$): $t = t_1 + t_2$.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nDepth h = 80 m, g = 10 m/s\u00b2, speed of sound v_s = 320 m/s.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nt\u2081 = \u221a(2h / g), t\u2082 = h / v_s, t = t\u2081 + t\u2082\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Time for stone to fall to the water surface: t\u2081 = \u221a(2h / g) = \u221a(2 \u00d7 80 / 10) = \u221a16 = 4 s.\n2. Time for the splash sound to travel up the well: t\u2082 = h / v_s = 80 / 320 = 0.25 s.\n3. Total time heard by observer at top: t = t\u2081 + t\u2082 = 4 + 0.25 = 4.25 s.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 4.25 s\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nClassic NEET trap: Don't forget that sound travels at a finite speed and takes time $h / v_s$ to reach the listener!",
